        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dcd399db-72bd-58a7-a03c-888f83b7d9ea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Kirby, Benny Goodman, O'Neill Spencer\n- Organizations: John Kirby Sextet\n- Songs: \"Loch Lomond\", \"Undecided\", \"The Bonnie Banks o' Loch Lomond\"\n- Topics: chamber jazz, jazz standards, Scottish music customs\n\nFacts:\n- In the late 1930s and early 1940s, John Kirby led a successful chamber jazz sextet.\n- John Kirby also worked as a sideman, prominently with Benny Goodman.\n- John Kirby's sextet recorded hit songs including \"Loch Lomond\" and the debut recording of \"Undecided\".\n- \"Undecided\" became a jazz standard.\n- O'Neill Spencer is best known for his work in the John Kirby Sextet.\n- In Scotland, \"The Bonnie Banks o' Loch Lomond\" is often played as the final piece of music at an evening of revelry.",
