        "text": "Page: John Kirby (musician). Sentence: In addition to sideman work (prominently with Benny Goodman), Kirby is remembered for leading a successful chamber jazz sextet in the late 1930s and early 1940s, which scored several hit songs including \"Loch Lomond\" and the debut recording of \"Undecided\", a jazz standard.\nPage: The Bonnie Banks o' Loch Lomond. Sentence: In Scotland, the song is often the final piece of music played during an evening of revelry (a dance party or dinner, etc.).\nPage: O'Neill Spencer. Sentence: He is most known for his work in the John Kirby Sextet.",
